WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:08.070
In this lesson, you will learn to use a repeat block to do the same moves many times and make code shorter.

2
00:00:08.070 --> 00:00:12.110
The repeat block does the blocks inside it again and again.

3
00:00:12.110 --> 00:00:19.070
The number on the repeat block says how many times.

4
00:00:19.070 --> 00:00:20.850
Repeat 3 does it three times.

5
00:00:20.850 --> 00:00:24.690
Stairs go right, up, right, up.

6
00:00:24.690 --> 00:00:27.370
Put “right, up” inside a repeat!

7
00:00:27.370 --> 00:00:29.570
A repeat makes long code short.

8
00:00:29.570 --> 00:00:31.670
Fewer blocks, same moves.

9
00:00:31.670 --> 00:00:38.160
Go right 6 squares. The arrow can only move 1, so use 🔁 repeat!

10
00:00:38.160 --> 00:00:41.230
Repeat 6 times: move right. Two blocks instead of six!

11
00:00:41.230 --> 00:00:45.910
Great work! Let’s remember what we learned.

12
00:00:45.910 --> 00:00:50.650
Now build along, then try the challenges. You’ve got this!
